# Peregrin Rules System — Skills + Digests + Full Rules

## How this works

This file is always in context. It contains 10 universal rules + a routing table.
Procedural rules are Devin Skills (`.agents/skills/`) — auto-activated by triggers.
Reference rules are compressed digests (`rules/.digest/`) — load on-demand per routing table.
Full rule files (`rules/`) are the source of truth — load when a digest lacks detail.

Each rule appears in exactly ONE place. No redundancy.

## Tier 0 — Universal Rules (always in context)

These apply to every line of code written. No exceptions.

- No `throw` in library code. OK in tests and `main.ts` only.
- Library functions return `Effect` for expected errors, never throw.
- Use `Effect.gen` + `yield*` for sequencing. Prefer `pipe` for linear transformations.
- Use `Schema` to validate at boundaries. Trust data once it has crossed a boundary.
- Discriminated unions over `string` when values are known. `Option`/`Either` over `null`/`undefined`.
- Functions are verbs, booleans are predicates (`is_`, `has_`), types are nouns.
- No abbreviations: `config` not `cfg`, `instance` not `inst`.
- Explicit over clever. `pipe(x, transform)` not `transform(x)` in a chain.
- Early returns over deep nesting. Max 3 levels. `if`/`else` guards at the top.
- Don't reinvent what exists — check Effect std-lib, workspace packages, then ecosystem.

## Skills (auto-activated)

Procedural rules live as Devin Skills in `.agents/skills/`. Devin auto-activates them based on task context.

| Skill | Triggers on |
|---|---|
| `git-conventions` | Committing, branching, PRs |
| `ci-cd` | CI config, pipeline changes, CI failures |
| `testing` | Writing tests, mocking, test structure |
| `create-package` | New package under `apps/` or `packages/` |
| `workspace-structure` | Workspace-level config, project layout |
| `write-adr` | Architecture decisions, design trade-offs |

## Digests (on-demand)

Load digests from `rules/.digest/` before starting work. If no row matches, Tier 0 is sufficient.

| Task involves | Load these digests |
|---|---|
| Effect idioms, `yield*`, `pipe` | `effect-conventions` |
| Error types, `Effect` error channel | `error-management` |
| Architecture, package structure, layering | `architecture` |
| Adding a dependency | `dependency-management` |
| Naming, nesting, function length | `code-style` |
| Choosing types, branded types, time | `data-types` |
| Comments, doc comments | `comments` |

Additional rule files can be added to `rules/` and `rules/.digest/` as the project grows.

## Digest → Full Rule Escalation

If a digest says "see <file>.md" or the task needs examples, code snippets, or full context —
load the full file from `rules/<file>.md`. Digests are reference cards; full files are source of truth.

## Sync

Run `scripts/check-digests.sh` to detect stale digests (source file modified after digest).
